document:
Provide Personal Protective Equipment to UK essential workers to fight Covid 19, In light of the UK spread of Covid 19 the government should mandate employers to: 
1) supply essential workers with Personal Protective Equipment;
2) introduce appropriate safety protocol in all workplaces, including social distancing between staff (and public), whether hospital or logistics hub., While some employers are already adopting basic measures and supplying minimal protective equipment this is still insufficiently widespread. It is illegal and immoral to put employees in a situation that undermines their health and safety. The government must act to supply employers with Personal Protective Equipment for all employees, and take all appropriate measures to make essential work safe. This will help slow transmission of the virus, and so avoid a humanitarian and economic disaster.

Commit to a public review of  HS2 project and suspend all on-going work now, A review of HS2 due to enormous changes in the last month, which significantly alter the basis on which the original decision was made.  

The review should consider data on anticipated journeys, demands on public expenditure, increased national debt and the potential impact of Covid 19., 1.	The pandemic has forced people to explore technology and the practicality of home working.  This could change the justification for HS2;
2.	The pandemic has highlighted investment needed in NHS. This  investment should take priority to HS2; 
3.	The country is incurring enormous costs as a result of the pandemic.  It is questioned we can now afford HS2; 
4.	Covid-19 has left a society shocked and emotionally shaken. The nation needs to heal; this project could lead to more division.

Close schools with confirmed COVID cases, 1. Close schools (where there is sovereignty to do so) until the 'second wave' is over;
2. Ensure that, when schools reopen, masks are worn and social distancing is recommended where possible;
3. Note with concern the sharp uptick in schools with COVID cases since 1/09/2020., As of the 18th September 2020, 1230 UK schools now have confirmed Coronavirus infections. This is incredibly concerning not only as it is representative of a rise in national cases, but also as it threatens the health and lives of pupils and their families. 

If we are to do everything that is feasibly possible to reduce the impact of COVID-19 upon the nation, then we must close schools to curb the size of the second wave.

I urge the Government to act as soon as is feasibly possible.
